WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:05.171
-My next guest is a great actor,
a 16-time WWE world champion

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.805
and a best-selling author.

00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:09.242
You can also see him
in a Super Bowl commercial

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.277
for Mountain Dew Major Melon.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:14.113
Here is John Cena!

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:16.315
[ Laughs ]

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:17.550
Wow!

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.519
-Hello, Jimmy Fallon!
-Wow, John!

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.956
This is unbelievable.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:23.990
I knew that you were
going to do something.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.791
-This is my job.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:27.960
-This is your --
Wait, I love it.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.896
This is Peacemaker?

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.466
-This is the first actual
interview that Peacemaker

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.268
has ever done, and I wanted to
bestow it upon you,

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:38.805
and it's
a really special occasion.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.640
So thanks for having me, man.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.576
I love being there in person,
but because we're miles away,

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.544
I wanted to --
I wanted Peacemaker to show up.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:46.846
-Wait, I love this. Wait.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.115
I have so many questions
because this is --

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.650
We talked last time
you were here.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.451
You were our first guest
in studio, by the way.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.120
Thank you for doing that.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.092
And you said you're doing a
spin-off series for Peacemaker,

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.761
and here you are as --
Are you on set?

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.431
-Yeah, so this is
actually Peacemaker's house,

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.968
and on the contrary, Peacemaker
was like a polar opposite

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.469
of Bruce Wayne,
where Bruce Wayne

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:12.571
would be a billionaire
with a bat cave.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:17.042
I live in a single-wide
and this is my outfit.

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:22.715
So it's a bit of an interesting
story and a bit of a new tale.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.319
-How do you describe
this character?

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.822
-I would say like a douchey,
bro-y Captain America.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:32.925
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.461
I love it. Can you show --

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.096
Do you have pants?
Do you have a cape?

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.164
What do you have?

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.866
-Oh, dude, if you want it
to get weird,

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.634
I'll show you the full piece.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.302
Is this what you want?
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:44.503
No, no, I don't want to
get weird.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.505
No, no, I don't want to
get weird.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.509
This is unbelievable.
I love that you did this.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.911
That comes out in August, right,
"The Suicide Squad"?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:56.182
-Yes, in August, and then
"Peacemaker" will be out

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.284
shortly after that on HBO Max.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:01.320
-I heard this rumor about you
in the movie --

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.622
and let me know if it's true --

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:05.859
that one of the most difficult
scenes in the movie

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.928
involved you eating an empanada.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.462
We have a photo of some --
-Oh, man.

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:13.332
The stunts were incredible

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.301
and filming the movie
was treacherous,

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.637
but that right there
is the face of defeat.

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:23.075
That is me eating
my 37th of 40 empanadas.

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:27.746
We had to do this one big take
because the horribly beautiful,

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:30.216
corrupted mind of
James Gunn operates

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.586
in so many intricate pieces,
and he wanted this big, giant

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.388
take where I thought
it'd be cool to like,

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.723
"Oh, it'd be funny
to eat the whole empanada.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.925
Throw the thing over my
shoulder, the guy catches it.

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:40.960
It's gonna be great.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.494
Everybody's gonna
think it's awesome."

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.831
I had to do it 40 times
and nearly ate myself sick,

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.333
and you can tell by that picture
I was not having a good day.

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:50.669
That was my most difficult stunt
in "The Suicide Squad."

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:52.272
-Could we see that photo
one more time?

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.273
It's just such a good photo.
It has to just --

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.743
[ Laughs ]
Oh, my God. Is that number 38?

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.278
-If that doesn't turn out
to be some sort of meme,

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:00.980
then the meme culture is dead!

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.916
-[ Laughs ]
Exactly, right?

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.485
John, I read that last year
was the first year

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:09.121
that you weren't able to
compete in WWE Raw

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:13.626
since 2004,
but you will be back, right?

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.829
-Yeah, I will.
I just, unfortunately, you know,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.364
the state of the world, I mean,
I'm not sitting there

00:03:19.364 --> 00:03:20.633
on the couch next to you.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.969
It's a difficult
and unpredictable time,

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.270
and right now I'm doing this.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.640
I'm filming "Peacemaker,"
and that's going to take a lot

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.009
of my time and I can't
bounce back and forth

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.577
due to
international restrictions.

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:35.615
So at least for the time being,
I'm here,

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.850
and I'm still away from WWE,

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.885
but I very much
look forward to returning

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.520
as soon as I possibly can.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.157
-You really are one of
the hardest working guys I know.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.325
In the middle of everything
you're doing,

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:49.829
you're also in a Super Bowl
commercial this year.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.264
I want to talk about
this commercial

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.333
because it's for the new
Mountain Dew Major Melon,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.736
and this is your second --
this is your second --

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.338
-Yeah, man, let's talk about it.

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:00.473
-This is your second
Super Bowl commercial.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.808
And it's just interesting to me.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:05.078
-I know,
back-to-back Super Bowls.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.713
I mean, this is incredible,
second Super Bowl commercial.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:09.448
This is great.

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:11.584
-I mean, I hate to cut you off
and everything like that,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:16.688
but last year I asked you to be
in a Super Bowl commercial

00:04:16.688 --> 00:04:19.458
with me and this year,
you're in a commercial.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.660
I just find it interesting
that, uh...

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.396
[ Laughs ] That you didn't
ask me to be in it.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:25.998
-Oh, yeah! No, no, no.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.469
So, long story short,
Mountain Dew Major Melon

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.736
came to me and said,
"You know what?

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.571
We want to do this awesome
Super Bowl commercial

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.740
that's gonna reinvent
advertising and the way

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.242
people watch the big game.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.077
Who do you want
your sidekick to be?"

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.279
I said, "Of course, I want it
to be Jimmy Fallon."

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:43.882
They said, "We can do that
or we can give away,

00:04:43.882 --> 00:04:45.518
on behalf of
Mountain Dew Major Melon,

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.853
a million dollars
and change somebody's life."

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:51.157
So I thought to myself,
"What would Jimmy Fallon do?

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.092
Jimmy Fallon
is a man of the people.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.861
Jimmy Fallon would want to
change someone's life."

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:58.130
Jimmy, don't you want to
give someone

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.733
the chance to win
a million dollars?

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.835
-Yes!

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:06.205
-Yeah, so screw you being in
the Super Bowl commercial.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:09.676
You're the man that's gonna
be the vehicle to give somebody

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:12.444
a million dollars if they can
identify all the bottles of

00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:15.615
Mountain Dew Major Melon
in the big game's commercial.

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.650
-Now, okay.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.718
I feel a little bit better
about this.

00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:22.921
So basically what you're saying
is if you watch the commercial

00:05:22.921 --> 00:05:25.992
during the Super Bowl
and you have to count how many

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.761
Major Melon bottles
are in the commercial?

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.464
If you can count them and --
-This one's a layup.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.966
Everyone's already gonna be
watching the Super Bowl.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.068
Watch the Mountain Dew
Major Melon commercial

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.370
because you're gonna be watching
all of the commercials,

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.839
count the number of
Mountain Dew Major Melon bottles

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:43.142
that you see, post it, and tag
Mountain Dew's Twitter handle.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:46.545
And if you're right,
you can win a million dollars,

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:50.516
and that's, in a long way,
thanks to you, Jimmy Fallon.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.683
-Wow.
-Thanks to you.

00:05:51.683 --> 00:05:53.419
-I just want to say I'm honored

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:56.155
and I can't wait to see
what I do.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.456
-You're gonna change
somebody's life.

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:58.490
-Yeah.
-You're gonna change

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.159
somebody's life.
-See?

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.661
-Jimmy Fallon giving away
a million bucks.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:05.197
-I love you and I love that
you're doing this.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:06.933
Do you want to play a game
when we come back?

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.801
-I would love to!
-Here we go.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.602
-I don't know how you're gonna
slap me with a fish,

00:06:10.602 --> 00:06:12.371
me being 3,000 miles away,

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:13.806
but, yes, I'll play a game
with you.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.708
-More with John Cena
after the break.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.543
Stick around, everybody.

